{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"partition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"by"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"belongsInSecondPartition"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:SK7ElementQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BidirectionalCollection\/Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:SK5IndexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BidirectionalCollection\/Index"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A predicate used to partition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the collection. All elements satisfying this predicate are ordered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after all elements not satisfying it."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"belongsInSecondPartition"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The index of the first element in the reordered collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that matches ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If no elements in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection match ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the returned index is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal to the collection’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After partitioning a collection, there is a pivot index ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no element before ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" satisfies the ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"predicate and every element at or after ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" satisfies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This operation isn’t guaranteed to be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stable, so the relative ordering of elements within the partitions might","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the following example, an array of numbers is partitioned by a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"predicate that matches elements greater than 30."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var numbers = [30, 40, 20, 30, 30, 60, 10]","let p = numbers.partition(by: { $0 > 30 })","\/\/ p == 5","\/\/ numbers == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30, 60, 40]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"numbers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array is now arranged in two partitions. The first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"partition, ","type":"text"},{"code":"numbers[..<p]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is made up of the elements that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are not greater than 30. The second partition, ","type":"text"},{"code":"numbers[p...]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is made up of the elements that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"are","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" greater than 30.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let first = numbers[..<p]","\/\/ first == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30]","let second = numbers[p...]","\/\/ second == [60, 40]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that the order of elements in both partitions changed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That is, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"40"},{"text":" appears before ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"60"},{"text":" in the original collection,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but, after calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"partition(by:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"60"},{"type":"text","text":" appears before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"40"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of the collection."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"partition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"by","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SK7ElementQa"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"ty